WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:07.200
it's Michelle from Lab muffin beauty
science here chemistry nerd and owner of

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.490
pink hair I've always wanted unicorn
hair ever since the hair chalk craze of

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:16.260
2013 and so when all the Plexes came onto
the market and I could finally get this

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.930
sort of hair I was so excited but the
problem is I'm also really lazy so I

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:26.400
knew that if having this sort of pastel
hair would mean that I would have to

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.789
keep going to the hairdresser and doing
hair masks and all of that sort of stuff

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:33.930
I knew it just wasn't going to happen
so before I went off and bleached my

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:38.160
hair I did a lot of research to check if
I could actually keep it up because

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.329
bleaching hair is not cheap and I didn't
want to just throw my money away

00:00:42.329 --> 00:00:45.780
I've had this bleached hair since July
2018

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:50.489
so I've had it for about a year and a
half and so this is what works for me

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:55.110
this is the lazy girl's coloured hair care
routine if you like this sort of video

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.890
please click the like button subscribe
to my channel and click the notification

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.520
bell so you don't miss any videos also
leave me a comment telling me what else

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.909
you want me to talk about next so before
you go and get your hair bleached I

00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:08.670
think it's really important to make sure
you're getting it bleached the right way

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:12.659
firstly you want to minimize damage
because damaged hair is going to require

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:16.170
so much more upkeep so make sure your
hairdresser is using some sort of

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:20.520
bonding agent like olaplex
to keep your hair in as good a condition

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.290
as possible hair is dead and so once
it's damaged it's really hard to do any

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:30.119
sort of repair to it you can modify it
to make it less damaged or feel less

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.829
damaged or act like it's less damaged
but you can't really reverse the damage

00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:39.869
properly the other thing is the pattern
of bleaching you're getting done so if

00:01:39.869 --> 00:01:44.640
you want a full head of bleached hair
the hairdresser will bleach it right up

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:49.320
to the roots or even on the scalp the
problem with this for a lazy person is

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:54.119
that when it grows out it will be like a
line and so once it gets to about there

00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:57.240
you have to go back to the hairdresser
and redo the roots or redo it yourself I

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.860
knew that that was just not going to
happen with me and so I got my

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:07.649
hairdresser to bleach it in what's
called a balayage or a blended root that

00:02:07.649 --> 00:02:12.370
means that the amount of each hair that
gets bleached is not quite the same so

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:16.239
it's lots of different lengths that
means that when it grows out it will

00:02:16.239 --> 00:02:19.959
grow out as this sort of blended
gradient rather than a harsh line the

00:02:19.959 --> 00:02:23.560
downside to this is that if you want to
get your hair rebleached if you want to

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:27.310
redo the growth it's really really
difficult for the hairdresser to do that

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.940
without rebleaching bits that are already
bleached and that will probably cause

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:34.780
your hair to snap off so my
hairdresser pretty much said see you in

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:38.680
two years so because that's what I
wanted that was great but keep in mind

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:44.319
that if you are lazy you might not get
exactly the look you want another thing

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:50.260
that I think is really important for a
lazy upkeep style is the choice of colour

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:54.670
hair likes to go brassy and Asian hair
especially likes to go brassy really

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:59.170
quickly this is when it starts to look
orange and this means that warm colors

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:03.670
are going to be a lot easier to keep
than cool colors I started with a really

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:08.019
cool purple which I loved but it
required me to shampoo my hair with

00:03:08.019 --> 00:03:11.500
purple shampoo twice a week it would
actually start to grow brassy around Day

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.980
4 so even if I wasn't planning to
wash my hair I had to just spray it with

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.269
tons and tons of purple spray now that I
have a warmer color it actually works

00:03:19.269 --> 00:03:22.630
really well what you do is you mix the
dye so that it's a little bit cooler

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:25.930
than what you actually watched and the
brassiness will actually add the warmth

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.690
for you and so it sort of blends in the
brassiness

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:32.349
it makes it look like it's intentional
another important thing to do is to pick

00:03:32.349 --> 00:03:36.819
a colour that looks good as it fades out
in general pinks and purples look nice

00:03:36.819 --> 00:03:40.840
greens and blues tend to look less nice
but it really depends on the specific

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:45.459
dye you're using so what I recommend is
looking up reviews and photos of what

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:48.849
the colour looks like as it fades so that
you can make sure that it's a colour

00:03:48.849 --> 00:03:53.079
you're happy with so that if you do get
lazy you're not stuck with a nasty colour

00:03:53.079 --> 00:03:56.799
you're not into if you're really
committed to a particular colour it might

00:03:56.799 --> 00:04:00.730
be a good idea to pick a dye that stains
your hair so again you can look this up

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:05.199
in reviews the problem is if you then
want to change your hair color you might

00:04:05.199 --> 00:04:08.500
have to do something that will damage
your hair at least a little bit you

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:13.060
might have to bleach it or do what I did
which was use Katie's direct dye fading

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:17.979
method which was gentler than bleach but
it still did cause a bit of damage you

00:04:17.979 --> 00:04:20.950
can see me doing that method in a video
tutorial I'll link that in the

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:24.580
description another important thing to
think about is how bright your hair

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.690
colour is
generally the brighter it is the more

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:32.070
fuss it is so if you have bright hair it
tends to bleed dye everywhere it bleeds

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:36.270
it into towels it bleeds it onto
light-colored sofas and chairs that you

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:40.320
lean on when your hair is wet it might
also stain white clothes if you ever

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.260
want to go into a float tank then you'll
have to wait until your hair stops

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:47.040
bleeding otherwise you might have to pay
a massive cleanup fee and your shower

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.970
can get quite stained as well pastel
colors are usually a bit safer because

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:55.080
there's just less dye there to bleed out
they can also help you save a bit on

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.620
hair dye because if you're using
temporary colour you can just dilute it

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:02.580
with white hair conditioner which is
pretty cheap I also redye my hair

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:06.450
every time I wash my hair using a dye
conditioner and I think this is probably

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:12.330
the number one thing that saved me time
in this whole hair routine journey the

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:16.200
product I use for this is this hair dye
which dyes your hair in three minutes

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:20.700
it's a Korean brand called espesso plus
now my friend was doing bright pink hair

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:24.630
and he complained that this would stain
his shower so bad but since I'm doing

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:29.250
more pastel I just dilute this into hair
conditioner and I don't have this

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:33.000
problem as much before I was using a dye
conditioner I was just redyeing my

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.650
hair once every 2 or 3 weeks it would
take about 45 minutes to apply the dye

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:41.340
during this time I listened to a podcast
so it wasn't like I was completely

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:46.229
wasting my time and then I would sit
around for maybe four hours and then

00:05:46.229 --> 00:05:50.070
rinse it out afterwards one of the
brands I really liked for this is brite

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:53.669
organix the nice thing about these
temporary hair dyes is that they don't

00:05:53.669 --> 00:05:56.639
tend to damage your hair so you can
leave it on for as long as you like

00:05:56.639 --> 00:05:59.820
they're just conditioners if you leave
it the longer it does tend to stain your

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:03.120
hair though if that's a problem for you
so now I use a dye conditioner I

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:07.289
dilute this into hair conditioner in a
lush tub and then I apply it onto my

00:06:07.289 --> 00:06:11.220
hair like it's hair conditioner by the
time I've worked the conditioner through

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:16.410
my hair and untangled all my hair with
my fingers it's about three minutes and

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:20.160
so once I rinse it off I get the color I
want the downside of course is that

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:23.490
you're using a lot more dye because a
lot less if it gets into your hair a lot

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:28.410
more of it goes down the drain but I am
happy to sacrifice that small amount of

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:34.229
money for the massive convenience it is
I also use a purple shampoo about once a

00:06:34.229 --> 00:06:38.310
fortnight even though my hair is this
warm color it does sometimes get a

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:42.150
little bit too warm and
orange and so this tones it down a bit

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:45.540
my favorite purple shampoo so far is
this one the fudge professional clean

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:49.560
blonde violet toning shampoo I really
like it because a lot of purple shampoos

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:52.740
tend to be really drying and so it
leaves your hair feeling like straw and

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:56.610
it's really difficult to untangle this
one does not which is great it's still

00:06:56.610 --> 00:07:02.160
really really pigmented though so you do
still get a lot of cooling with very

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.850
little effort if you've read my blog
you'll know that I am a massive fan of

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:10.860
amodimethicone this has been such a game
changer ingredient for my hair it is

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:14.340
probably the number one thing that my
hair can't live without now before I

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:18.300
bleached my hair it wasn't that impressive
but now that I have it is so different

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:22.350
from all the other silicones there are
two things that make amodimethicone

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:27.180
really really cool firstly it has a
positive charge what this means is that

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:31.530
it will bind to more damaged regions of
your hair which tend to have a more

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:36.540
negative charge secondly it means that
it doesn't form a really thick film that

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:40.020
weighs down your hair once you have
enough amodimethicone on your hair

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:44.820
the positive charge is quite positive
and so anymore amodimethicone will be

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:48.090
repelled because like charges repel I
didn't really have a problem with

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:51.600
dimethicone before I bleached my hair
but after I bleached my hair I found

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:54.930
that it tends to weigh my hair down
quite a lot secondly amodimethicone

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:58.920
forms a film that lasts through several
washes if you're trying to treat your

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:03.540
hair with a treatment like olaplex then
maybe this isn't so good but I found

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:08.490
that it really does protect your hair in
between you doing things to it and so

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:12.990
you still get that detangling you still
get the lack of snags which is really

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:16.470
important because that's what causes
permanent damage that can't be reversed

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:21.330
I had a few products that I really liked
that contain amodimethicone but as my

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:24.870
luck would have it they were
discontinued and so I've been looking

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:29.130
for new products these are the ones I
found which work there's the Elizavecca

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:33.930
CER 100 collagen ceramide coating
protein treatment it does have protein

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:37.950
in it but the main star in this is
probably the amodimethicone the best

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.490
drugstore conditioner that I found which
has amodimethicone is this one

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:45.510
which I just found out has been
