the thing I like about this is that it

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:22.029
works really well on dry hair so on day
two or three if you realize you didn't

00:09:22.029 --> 00:09:26.380
get quite enough detangling into your
hair you can just spray it on don't

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:30.130
touch it for a bit let it dry off and
then it goes really really silky and

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:34.600
again lots of amodimethicone another
brand that I've recently found is

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:38.709
Kerastase which has lots of products
that contain amodimethicone high in

00:09:38.709 --> 00:09:42.940
the ingredients list I also use olaplex
on my hair olaplex number three is

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:47.050
the take home version I treat my hair
want about once a month with it it's

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:50.320
meant to repair sulfur sulfur bonds so if
you have broken sulfur sulfur bonds it

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:55.449
puts them back in place sort of I used
to use this a lot more but ever since I

00:09:55.449 --> 00:10:00.040
discovered amodimethicone I found that
I don't actually need to some people say

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:03.519
that silicones cover up the damage but
to be honest that's what all

00:10:03.519 --> 00:10:08.920
conditioners do they cover up the damage
nothing truly repairs damage the

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.670
important thing about conditioners is
that they do cover up the damage but

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:16.209
they also prevent further damage they
lubricate your hair so that when it

00:10:16.209 --> 00:10:20.620
slides past it doesn't chip away at the
cuticle I found that without using

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:24.430
silicones I get so much more breakage
and split ends that it's not worth

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:28.420
avoiding them for me when I do do an
olaplex treatment I try to avoid using

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:32.769
amodimethicone for a couple of washes
beforehand so that it gets rid of most

00:10:32.769 --> 00:10:37.060
of the film and the olaplex can
penetrate through but a lot of the time

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:41.050
I found that my hair just gets really
nasty and unmanageable and I get more

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:44.889
split ends during that phase so that's
probably why I use the olaplex a lot

00:10:44.889 --> 00:10:50.230
less now because that is just too much
to sacrifice because I've been trying to

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:54.639
wash my hair a bit less but I am still
quite oily I found that dry shampoo is

00:10:54.639 --> 00:10:58.600
really important
my favorite dry shampoo is probably the

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:03.160
batiste dry shampoo just because it is
strong enough to soak up my oil without

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:06.819
